{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>YHWH, YHWH.</b> This is the attribute of mercy — one before a person sins, and one after he sins and returns (Rosh HaShanah 17)." "<b>El.</b> This too is an attribute of mercy, and so it says: ״אֵלִי אֵלִי לָמָה עֲזַבְתָּנִי״ (Psalms 22) — and one would not say to the attribute of justice, 'why have you forsaken me'; thus I found in Mekhilta." "<b>Slow to anger.</b> He lengthens His anger and does not hasten to punish — perhaps he will do teshuvah." "<b>And abundant kindness.</b> To those who need kindness — for they do not have that many merits." "<b>And truth.</b> To pay good reward to those who do His will."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:29.011623657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}